Subject: Widen the short expiry window in TestSessionExpireAt

Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Raise the expiry offset in TestSessionExpireAt from 100 microseconds to 500 milliseconds so the session is not already expired when the following Get runs on a loaded builder.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb db5102ec64d5dd3dfa87208edb054eb0721c36c9
Verify: cmd `go test ./inmem -run TestSessionExpireAt -count=1` expect "ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (test-only change for the build environment)
Drop-When: never: upstream sets a 100 microsecond expiry and calls Get immediately, which races on a slow builder

Upstream sets a 100 microsecond future expiry and then immediately calls Get. Under scheduler latency the session can appear expired before Get runs. The assertion is unchanged; only the window is wider.

diff --git a/inmem/session_store_test.go b/inmem/session_store_test.go
index d4fb46e..3ded7d0 100644
--- a/inmem/session_store_test.go
+++ b/inmem/session_store_test.go
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ func TestSessionExpireAt(t *testing.T) {
 		t.Fatal(err)
 	}
 
-	if err := st.ExpireAt("yo", time.Now().Add(100*time.Microsecond)); err != nil {
+	if err := st.ExpireAt("yo", time.Now().Add(500*time.Millisecond)); err != nil {
 		t.Fatal(err)
 	}
 
